  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "43340720",
      "title": "Why Use A Separate Backend? Fetching Directly From The Source!",
      "lectureOrder": 161,
      "videoOrder": 149,
      "sourceHash": "cbe7fdfdbc4236d70b65b32a44c3d73b196b48538458a855cc188a8bb2025032",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0,
          "end": 2.7,
          "en": "[Maximilian Schwarzmuller] So we're now fetching data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 2.7,
          "end": 7.26,
          "en": "directly on the server inside of the React Server Component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.26,
          "end": 10.65,
          "en": "and that's better than doing it on the client side.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.65,
          "end": 13.89,
          "en": "But if you have a situation as we have it here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.89,
          "end": 17.61,
          "en": "where you also own that separate backend",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 17.61,
          "end": 19.83,
          "en": "that provides the data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 19.83,
          "end": 24.42,
          "en": "you have to ask yourself why you split your application",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 24.42,
          "end": 27.93,
          "en": "into two servers in the first place.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 27.93,
          "end": 31.2,
          "en": "Why do we have a separate backend server here?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 31.2,
          "end": 35.55,
          "en": "Why don't we instead directly reach out to the database",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 35.55,
          "end": 38.583,
          "en": "from inside our Next.js application?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 39.63,
          "end": 43.2,
          "en": "And of course, there might be reasons for that extra server,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 43.2,
          "end": 45.78,
          "en": "but here in our demo, in this scenario,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 45.78,
          "end": 48.06,
          "en": "there is no such reason.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 48.06,
          "end": 49.95,
          "en": "And hence, as a next step,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 49.95,
          "end": 53.52,
          "en": "we can even get rid of this fetch call here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 53.52,
          "end": 56.79,
          "en": "and of sending this extra HTTP request,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 56.79,
          "end": 59.4,
          "en": "and instead move that database",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 59.4,
          "end": 64.29,
          "en": "from that separate backend server into our Next.js project.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 64.29,
          "end": 66.72,
          "en": "So I'll just move that data.db file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 66.72,
          "end": 69.6,
          "en": "into this Next.js project",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 69.6,
          "end": 72.42,
          "en": "and add some code to that Next.js project",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 72.42,
          "end": 76.32300000000001,
          "en": "that does allow us to directly reach out to that database.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 77.43,
          "end": 80.28,
          "en": "For that, I'll stop that backend server,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 80.28,
          "end": 84.09,
          "en": "and then go back into my root Next.js project folder.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 84.09,
          "end": 86.88,
          "en": "And I'll start by adding an extra dependency",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 86.88,
          "end": 90.6,
          "en": "that will allow us to reach out to that database.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 90.6,
          "end": 93.12299999999999,
          "en": "And that dependency is called better-sqlite3.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 94.77000000000001,
          "end": 97.77000000000001,
          "en": "That's a package that allows us to easily interact",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 97.77000000000001,
          "end": 99.66,
          "en": "with a SQLite database,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 99.66,
          "end": 102.783,
          "en": "as we have it here with that data.db file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 104.28,
          "end": 108.27000000000001,
          "en": "Then as a next step, I'll go to this lib folder,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 108.27000000000001,
          "end": 110.28,
          "en": "and there, the news.js file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 110.28,
          "end": 113.043,
          "en": "where we're currently using the dummy news.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 114.03,
          "end": 115.95,
          "en": "And I'll keep that around for now",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 115.95,
          "end": 118.68,
          "en": "so that the entire app doesn't break suddenly.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 118.68,
          "end": 122.1,
          "en": "But I'll also add a new import here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 122.1,
          "end": 126.483,
          "en": "and I'll name it SQL and import this better-sqlite3 package.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 127.65,
          "end": 131.34,
          "en": "And then here, I'll initialize access to my database",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 131.34,
          "end": 134.22,
          "en": "by creating a db variable or a constant,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 134.22,
          "end": 137.7,
          "en": "and by calling this SQL thing I'm importing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 137.7,
          "end": 139.68,
          "en": "from better-sqlite3.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 139.68,
          "end": 141.32999999999998,
          "en": "And then we pass a path",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 141.32999999999998,
          "end": 145.56,
          "en": "to our database file seen from the root project folder",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 145.56,
          "end": 147.27,
          "en": "to this function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 147.27,
          "end": 150.32999999999998,
          "en": "So my database file is called data.db,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 150.32999999999998,
          "end": 152.763,
          "en": "so it's data.db which I add here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 153.9,
          "end": 157.47,
          "en": "And yes, it's not in the same folder as the news.js folder,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 157.47,
          "end": 159.09,
          "en": "but here, you add a path",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 159.09,
          "end": 161.57999999999998,
          "en": "that is relative to the root project folder,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 161.57999999999998,
          "end": 165.513,
          "en": "and data.db is stored in that root project folder.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 166.56,
          "end": 169.92000000000002,
          "en": "This will then give us access to that database.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 169.92000000000002,
          "end": 174.21,
          "en": "And now I'll start with this getAllNews function here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 174.21,
          "end": 176.67000000000002,
          "en": "And instead of returning my dummy news here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 176.67000000000002,
          "end": 180.243,
          "en": "I wanna return news that are fetched from that database.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 181.08,
          "end": 185.79,
          "en": "And for that, we can use that db constant here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 185.79,
          "end": 189.33,
          "en": "and call prepare to prepare a new SQL statement",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 189.33,
          "end": 191.43,
          "en": "that should be executed,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 191.43,
          "end": 194.343,
          "en": "and simply select everything from news.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 195.21,
          "end": 197.61,
          "en": "And of course, you don't need to know SQL",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 197.61,
          "end": 200.01,
          "en": "to follow along with this course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 200.01,
          "end": 203.85,
          "en": "We'll just write some basic statements and commands here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 203.85,
          "end": 206.34,
          "en": "and you can simply copy and paste them.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 206.34,
          "end": 208.02,
          "en": "You don't need to know SQL.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 208.02,
          "end": 210.54,
          "en": "Using it is, of course, absolutely optional",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 210.54,
          "end": 212.43,
          "en": "when working with Next.js.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 212.43,
          "end": 213.93,
          "en": "And I'm just using it here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 213.93,
          "end": 218.073,
          "en": "because I chose to use SQLite as a demo database.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 219.39,
          "end": 221.28,
          "en": "Now, we then have to call the all method",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 221.28,
          "end": 222.75,
          "en": "on this prepared statement",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 222.75,
          "end": 227.1,
          "en": "to essentially return and store all the returned data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 227.1,
          "end": 229.53,
          "en": "in that news constant.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 229.53,
          "end": 231.84,
          "en": "So that will then be an array of news items",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 231.84,
          "end": 233.913,
          "en": "that are fetched from that database.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 235.02,
          "end": 237.9,
          "en": "And these news items will have the same structure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 237.9,
          "end": 241.11,
          "en": "as the news we had in the dummy news constant,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 241.11,
          "end": 244.05,
          "en": "because in that backend code where I had the code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 244.05,
          "end": 246.12,
          "en": "for initializing that database,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 246.12,
          "end": 249.513,
          "en": "I made sure that the same structure was set up there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 251.37,
          "end": 252.9,
          "en": "So with that, I'm getting all the news,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 252.9,
          "end": 254.94,
          "en": "and now we can return them",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 254.94,
          "end": 259.94,
          "en": "because the nice thing about this better-sqlite3 package",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 259.95,
          "end": 263.91,
          "en": "is that it's actually giving us asynchronous API.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 263.91,
          "end": 266.19,
          "en": "So this does not even yield a promise",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 266.19,
          "end": 267.66,
          "en": "which we have to await.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 267.66,
          "end": 270.03,
          "en": "Instead, we can just execute the code like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 270.03,
          "end": 273.12,
          "en": "and will instantly get the news that were fetched,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 273.12,
          "end": 274.98,
          "en": "which of course is pretty convenient",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 274.98,
          "end": 278.04,
          "en": "because that means that this is all we have to do here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 278.04,
          "end": 279.813,
          "en": "in order to fetch our news.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 281.4,
          "end": 285.09000000000003,
          "en": "And in page.js where we need those news,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 285.09000000000003,
          "end": 289.02,
          "en": "we can now get rid of all this data fetching code here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 289.02,
          "end": 292.95,
          "en": "and instead just get our news by calling getAllNews,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 292.95,
          "end": 295.743,
          "en": "which is imported from that news file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 297.54,
          "end": 299.88,
          "en": "And if we now save that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 299.88,
          "end": 301.5,
          "en": "and we reload,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 301.5,
          "end": 304.35,
          "en": "boom, our news are there again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 304.35,
          "end": 306.93,
          "en": "And of course, hopefully, unsurprisingly,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 306.93,
          "end": 309.18,
          "en": "they are there in the code that was rendered",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 309.18,
          "end": 310.62,
          "en": "on the server as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 310.62,
          "end": 313.8,
          "en": "And now we skip that extra backend",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 313.8,
          "end": 316.68,
          "en": "and that extra HTTP round-trip.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 316.68,
          "end": 320.58,
          "en": "And instead, we directly fetch data from the data source,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 320.58,
          "end": 322.41,
          "en": "which in this case is a database,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 322.41,
          "end": 325.05,
          "en": "but which could also be a file or whatever.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 325.05,
          "end": 327.78,
          "en": "And we directly fetch data from there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 327.78,
          "end": 329.7,
          "en": "and use that in our components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 329.7,
          "end": 332.58,
          "en": "And that's, of course, a really nice feature",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 332.58,
          "end": 334.2,
          "en": "which we can only use",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 334.2,
          "end": 337.53,
          "en": "because we have those React Server Components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 337.53,
          "end": 341.67,
          "en": "because that database, of course, lives on our server.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 341.67,
          "end": 345.06,
          "en": "This code would not work on the client side",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 345.06,
          "end": 347.52,
          "en": "because the client side doesn't have access",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 347.52,
          "end": 348.63,
          "en": "to that database.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 348.63,
          "end": 351.96,
          "en": "And it shouldn't for security reasons.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 351.96,
          "end": 354.42,
          "en": "But since we're in the React Server Component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 354.42,
          "end": 359.07,
          "en": "this code will only ever execute on the server,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 359.07,
          "end": 360.75,
          "en": "unlike client components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 360.75,
          "end": 362.94,
          "en": "which also execute on the client.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 362.94,
          "end": 365.76,
          "en": "But this code only executes on the server,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 365.76,
          "end": 368.25,
          "en": "and therefore we can safely reach out",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 368.25,
          "end": 372.003,
          "en": "to that server site database and get our data from there.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
